Lobium - WebGL vendor/renderer, scalar caps, and pixel farbling (seeds.webgl).

Split out of core/config-channel.patch. Two further WebGL patches build on this one and must apply
AFTER it: fingerprint/host-gpu-profile.patch (version / shadingLanguageVersion / extensions /
shaderPrecision) and fingerprint/webgl-runtime-safety.patch (never advertise a capability the
active backend cannot execute).

  * UNMASKED_VENDOR_WEBGL / UNMASKED_RENDERER_WEBGL, overridden as an ATOMIC PAIR so a persona can
    never report one real and one spoofed half.
  * The scalar MAX_* capability set, so the numbers agree with the claimed renderer string instead
    of leaking the real (or software) backend's limits.
  * Per-profile WebGL PIXEL FARBLING. gl.readPixels returns a BOTTOM-UP buffer, while the WebGL
    toDataURL/toBlob snapshot is top-down; both are farbled on a shared TOP-DOWN key
    (FarbleCanvasRgbaFlippedRows for the former), so two profiles on the same GPU get
    distinct-but-stable WebGL pixel hashes AND a detector cross-checking readPixels against the
    encoded image sees consistent noise rather than a contradiction.
    Scope: default framebuffer, RGBA/UNSIGNED_BYTE, default pack state.

Hook point: third_party/blink/renderer/modules/webgl/webgl_rendering_context_base.cc.

